  "post_extraction_changes": "index.html has separate notification center content, a usable admin compose/send form, personalized shopper lists/coupon views, working activity filters, consumer/vendor reviews and linked payment verification, vendor-specific search, an interactive business card editor with persisted product-image upload/preview and QR display, linked vendor incident-report/admin ticket screens, a vendor data dashboard with selectable activity ranges, selectable vendor booth intentions, vendor-only event listing/detail/application screens, and manager event/check-in views backed by shared activity, vendor attendance and consumer check-in records; assets/js/app.js adds live local time, role/payment/incident notifications, shopper ranking, locally persisted coupons/reviews/payments/vendor card/product images/incident data/vendor booth preferences/event application intentions, activity filters/sorting, review and rating synchronization, payment verification synchronization, vendor management search, image compression/validation and business-card gallery display, QR generation, incident ticket status progression, shop-specific sample metrics and recommendations with period-specific activity scores, booth choice independent of recommendations, vendor-only registration filtering, shared activity publishing/signup controls, persistent consumer check-in with duplicate prevention, cross-role vendor attendance, and actionable manager check-in reminders in the vendor notification center. The original snapshot remains unchanged.",
  "javascript_syntax_check": "passed (node --check)",
  "browser_validation": "Existing consumer, vendor, payment, incident and product-image checks remain recorded. This update was browser-tested across two same-origin tabs: publishing an activity in manager view exposed it to vendor registration; closing its signup removed it from the vendor list; consumer event check-in persisted and updated the manager attendance count; vendor location check-in updated both manager and consumer event status without overwriting consumer records; and manager check-in reminders appeared in the vendor notification center and navigated to vendor sign-in. Duplicate consumer check-in was blocked. JavaScript syntax, editor diagnostics and git diff whitespace checks passed. Cross-device live sync is not available; same-origin localStorage is used.",
